{"name":"Blueberry Tart","hex":"#3f4050","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blueberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible round berry, belonging to the cowberry group (Vaccinium sect. Cyanococcus), with flared crowns at the end, that turns blue on ripening.","The shrub of the above-mentioned berry."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark blue colour.","Resembling or characteristic of blueberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blueberry"},{"term":"tart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sharp to the taste; acid; sour.","High or too high in acidity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of small open pie, or piece of pastry, now typically containing jelly (US) / jam (UK) or conserve, or sometimes other fillings (chocolate, custard, egg, butter, historically even meat or other savory fillings).","A melt (block of wax for use in a tart burner)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blueberry","blocks":[{"text":"Blueberries are a widely distributed and widespread group of perennial flowering plants with blue or purple berries. They are classified in the section Cyanococcus within the genus Vaccinium. Commercial blueberries—both wild (lowbush) and cultivated (highbush)—are all native to North America. The highbush varieties were introduced into Europe during the 1930s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Blueberries.jpg/330px-Blueberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blueberry","wikidata":"Q13178"},{"title":"Tart","blocks":[{"text":"A tart is a baked dish consisting of a filling over a pastry base with an open top not covered with pastry. The pastry is usually shortcrust pastry; the filling may be sweet or savoury, though modern tarts are usually fruit-based, sometimes with custard. Tartlet refers to a miniature tart; an example would be egg tarts. The categories of \"tart\", \"flan\", and \"pie\" overlap, with no sharp distinctions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Raspberry_tart.jpg/330px-Raspberry_tart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tart","wikidata":"Q1142483"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/500px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/1280px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/500px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blueberries showing various stages of maturation. IG = Immature Green, GP = Green Pink, BP = Blue Pink, and R = Ripe.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg/500px-Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg/1280px-Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg/500px-Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Whole blueberry and in cross-section","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th